course: dictionary
lesson: 14743
title: Words for the coast
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A promontory is a high point of land or rock that sticks out into the sea or a lake. Its shape gives you the clue: it juts out, like a finger pointing at the water.
explain: «The lighthouse stood on a rocky promontory, where it could warn ships far out at sea.» The clues are rocky, stood on, and warn ships at sea, so a promontory is land by the water. Test it: put headland in place of promontory, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Promontory has another meaning in science. In the body, it is a part that sticks out, like a bump on a bone. The spelling is the same, so the place where you meet the word tells you which meaning to use.
fact: A promontory is a high point of land or rock that sticks out into the sea or a lake.
fact: A promontory is another word for a headland.
fact: «A promontory overlooking the sea» means a high spot of land with a view of the water.
fact: In geography, waves help shape promontories along the coast over a very long time.
fact: In the body, a promontory is a part that sticks out, such as a bump on a bone.
exercise: «The old castle was built on a promontory above the sea.» What is a promontory? | A road that runs through a town | A small boat used for fishing | *A high point of land that sticks out into the sea | A deep, dark cave under the water
exercise: Mia said, «We walked out along the promontory and watched the waves crash below.» Where were they standing? | In a field far from any water | In a shop by the harbour | *On a high point of land sticking out over the water | Inside a deep, dark tunnel
exercise: Which word in «The lighthouse stood on a rocky promontory» means the same as headland? | rocky | stood | lighthouse | *promontory
test: Sam says a promontory is a kind of boat. What does promontory really mean? | A flat field of grass | *A high point of land or rock sticking out into the sea | A small boat with two sails | A deep hole in a river
test: In science, a promontory on a bone means what? | A hole where the bone has broken | A thin line that runs down the bone | A soft part that stretches and bends | *A part of the body that sticks out, like a bump on a bone
exam: «The sailors saw the lighthouse on the promontory long before they reached the shore.» What is a promontory? | A kind of sandy beach | *A high point of land that sticks out into the sea | A bridge over a river | A harbour for big ships
